title = Madagascar Hissing Cockroach
description = The Madagascar hissing cockroach (Gromphadorhina portentosa), also known as the hissing cockroach, Malagasy hissing cockroach or simply hisser, is one of the largest species of cockroach, reaching 5 to 7. 5 centimetres (2 to 3 inches) at maturity. They are native to the island of Madagascar, where they are commonly found in rotting logs.
